  "intro": "A ratio compares quantities; a rate is a ratio with different units (like miles per hour). Solve proportions by cross-multiplying: $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d}$ gives $ad=bc$. Unit conversion multiplies by conversion factors equal to $1$ (such as $\\frac{60\\text{ min}}{1\\text{ hr}}$) so the unwanted units cancel. On the SAT, track units carefully and set up the proportion so matching units align.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "If $3$ pens cost $\\$4.50$, how much do $7$ pens cost at the same rate?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Find the unit rate: $\\frac{4.50}{3}=1.50$ dollars per pen.",
          "Multiply by $7$: $1.50\\times 7=10.50$.",
          "So $7$ pens cost $\\$10.50$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\$10.50$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Solve the proportion $\\dfrac{x}{12}=\\dfrac{3}{4}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Cross-multiply: $4x=12\\cdot 3=36$.",
          "Divide by $4$: $x=9$."
        ],
        "answer": "$x=9$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Convert $2$ hours to seconds.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Use $1$ hour $=60$ minutes and $1$ minute $=60$ seconds.",
          "$2\\text{ hr}\\times 60\\times 60=2\\times 3600$.",
          "So $7200$ seconds."
        ],
        "answer": "$7200$ seconds"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "$5$ apples cost $\\$2$. Cost of $15$?",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$15$ is $3\\times 5$, so $3\\times \\$2=\\$6$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\$6$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
